From 03faef200d36ef19d392da5c0c9898c1619f663c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homar <homar@local>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:07:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] homalawn page reorder: edit-mode page reorder moves pages,
 with page thumbnails

Dragging a page in the edit-mode page strip (#6809) did two swaps that
cancelled out: movePageGroup swapped the page order (mScreenOrder,
saved as workspace_screen_order) and then also swapped the items'
screen ids in the database (moveWorkspaceScreensInDatabase), whose
bindItemsUpdated moved every item back to its old page. Only what is
bound to a page itself travelled: the search/date bar of screen 0 and
the default-home mark. The id swap could also put top-row items into
screen 0, where the loader reserves row 0 for the search bar and
deletes them as overlapping.

Now only the order changes: every CellLayout keeps its screen id, so a
page moves with all its items, screen 0 keeps the date bar (which
travels with its page), the default home page follows its page, and
the saved order puts it back after a restart. The item remap, its
strip-deferral flag and its two swap-map tests are removed.

The page strip: each chip shows a picture of its page (the page's
items recorded into a Picture and rendered by the GPU, so widgets with
hardware bitmaps draw too), made when the strip opens and after each
drag, with the home-page button in its corner; chips are keyed by
screen id; a move no longer rebinds the chip being dragged (which
ended the drag after one step); the strip is centred and fits five
pages on a 411 dp wide screen instead of truncated "Def..."/"Pag..."
labels with the fourth chip half off screen.
